---
description: Backend conventions
globs: backend/**/*.java
alwaysApply: false
---

Backend conventions:
- The backend uses Java and Spring Boot.
- Preserve the existing modular monolith structure.
- Respect module boundaries and existing dependencies.
- Follow the existing Controller -> Service -> Repository architecture.
- Keep controllers thin and business logic in services.
- Follow existing DTO, entity, mapper, validation, and exception-handling patterns.
- Use existing Spring Security and authorization mechanisms.
- Preserve tenant isolation and existing firm/client ownership rules.
- Do not trust tenant or authorization-sensitive identifiers supplied by the client when they can be derived from the authenticated user.
- Follow existing API response and error conventions.